{"id": "EUVD-2026-86220", "enisaUuid": "f1f89219-c778-379a-ae18-5903591542d7", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nASoC: rockchip: rockchip_pdm: Handle runtime PM resume failures in set_fmt\n\nrockchip_pdm_set_fmt() calls pm_runtime_get_sync() before accessing\nhardware registers, but ignores its return value.\nIf the runtime resume fails, the function continues to perform register\naccesses while the device state is undefined.\nReplace pm_runtime_get_sync() with pm_runtime_resume_and_get() and\nreturn early on failure to avoid unpowered register accesses.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T16:03:13", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-03T10:58:01", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/105ea8b7a29b473cbe3aa1e542997700c98e3adc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/aa48db0257ed4cdb52f922d32872dcc8d201925e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/52b77346cf66174ab9bc34504729cd686a9e29b1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7f0fd754c708785c31b067dd98649e3ec9b8fd72", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a9cc27a4a9b5fe013e152841fd8408061fa2312f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b2b5c2ca5a4924271fa86d75a252de32fa285375", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ee7b5f7b39332febf917f9ebf212842cc9379815"], "aliases": ["GHSA-c9v7-6fmw-v2g3", "CVE-2026-97407"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0ea743fb-1d9b-3a48-a529-215c4f48b851", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "138ab8bb-7b65-3012-9627-e2b7a0b1bfde", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.271"}, {"id": "252d3fb1-9d43-3543-a088-8451dd8f07da", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "255b7542-a872-39df-8e9a-886117a6e2cc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c85064435fe7a216ec0f0238ef2b8f7cd850a450 <aa48db0257ed4cdb52f922d32872dcc8d2